domain ADR0032:
  description "ADR-0032 revision 1: Bind V3 characters to versioned battles. Status Proposed."

problem P1:
  |
    The first V3-versus-V3 Stage trial requires new battles to freeze two V3
    character generations and carry their V4 compiler inputs through reload and
    all battle consumers. The existing startBattle path and manifest versions do
    not represent that tuple.

evidence E1:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0010 requires battle creation to read and bind exact compatible
    current generations without authoring writes. Accepted ADR-0030 defines
    CharacterBattleCompilerInputsV4 and character_generation_v3 provenance.
    Accepted ADR-0028 binds the complete dialogue-V3 compact projection,
    activation and psyche-reaction tuple and rejects mixed discriminators.

evidence E2:
  |
    At revision 067cb01, battle-service startBattle parses V2 envelopes and
    records character_generation_v2 and compilerInputsV2. Its manifest version
    3 upgrade changes the dialogue tuple while retaining V2 character sources.

evidence E3:
  |
    The owner selected two new V3 characters for the first Stage trial and
    excluded a V3-versus-V2 first battle. PERT vt101 owns registration and
    selection; vt102 owns battle binding and consumers; vt103 joins both.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Relabel manifest V3 as V3-character data, add a mixed-version union, or add
    one distinct all-V3 manifest variant. Relabeling changes historical meaning;
    mixed-version execution adds behavior the first trial does not need.

premise U1:
  |
    Before owner acceptance, this proposed manifest and consumer contract did
    not authorize implementation of its new persisted version. Stage writes
    remain separately authorized.

pending U2:
  |
    The V3 generation reader currently reports compatibility but does not
    itself reject blocked current generations. vt101 must supply and test the
    current-pointer/readiness boundary and the exact battle-required capability
    set before integrated creation can be claimed.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-18, after the exact English authoritative think, Markdown
    projection, complete Japanese review scope, alternatives, risks and
    unknowns were presented, the product owner replied ACCEPT for ADR-0032
    revision 1. The pre-acceptance authoritative SHA-256 was
    39fa661060cba238014836fca416ff819d80ce0c3b85ba9a60c7e08e6e8ce3ed.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, OPTIONS, U1, U2:
  |
    Propose a distinct BattleAssetManifestV4 for battles created with two V3
    character generations. Each side uses BattleCharacterAssetBindingV4: exact
    asset/generation identity, content digest, immutable combat-ready snapshot,
    character_generation_v3 basic-action provenance, and
    CharacterBattleCompilerInputsV4. Preserve ADR-0028's dialogue schema-3
    compact projection, activation identity, psyche-reaction-policy-v1,
    exact character digests and complete-tuple discrimination. The character
    compiler member advances from V3 to V4; other frozen asset/rule identities
    remain bound.

decision D2 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, OPTIONS, U1, U2:
  |
    Creation reads the current V3 generation for each character through the
    compatible current-pointer and readiness contract supplied by vt101, and
    fails closed for missing, mismatched, blocked-capability, or mixed-version
    generations. The exact battle-required capability set must match the V4
    consumers and be verified with vt101 before integrated creation. It does
    not append a generation, move a current pointer, invoke authoring, or
    silently convert a V2 character. Binding preparation may be implemented
    independently, but complete local creation proof waits for vt101.

decision D3 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, OPTIONS, U1, U2:
  |
    Battle execution, retry, reload, narration, presentation and observation
    consume the frozen V4 tuple. Execute V3 action norms as action selectors;
    keep conscious guidance out of the mechanical selector; apply registered
    fallback only after legality revalidation with its conflict receipt, as
    required by ADR-0030. Do not coerce V4 inputs to a V2/V3 norm program or
    reread mutable current character data as an authoritative input.

decision D4 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, OPTIONS, U1, U2:
  |
    Parse and persist the new variant without changing the meaning of existing
    manifest versions 1-3. Existing battles remain on their recorded manifest;
    no automatic migration or rebinding occurs. This decision covers the first
    all-V3 trial only and does not decide mixed-version battles, V2 migration,
    provider generation, Stage activation, or production promotion.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, D1, D2, D3, D4:
  |
    Accept exact ADR-0032 revision 1 as the all-V3 battle manifest and
    consumer decision. This authorizes implementation within vt102, but does
    not authorize Stage writes, release, mixed-version behavior, V2 migration,
    or a claim that local or Stage battle execution is complete.
